WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.559 --> 00:00:05.040
- [Interviewer] Hey, Jasmine.

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.320
Jasmine, where'd you grow up?

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:07.960
Where are you from originally?

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:10.420
- Well, I was born in Inglewood

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.820
but I wasn't born in the hospital

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:16.430
and then I ended up being
raised in the foster care system

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:19.350
because my mother passed away in '93.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:20.900
- [Interviewer] How old were you?

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:22.540
- I was a baby still

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:25.740
and I ended up living
with my grandmother first,

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.720
and they ended up taking me
at nine from my grandmother

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:30.170
because she was being abusive,

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.200
and they put me in the foster care system

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.810
from nine to 18.

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:38.350
But when I was a baby

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:42.260
I already had a CPS worker
and all that so yeah.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.070
- [Interviewer] So most
of your childhood was-

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:45.620
- Yes, foster-

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.010
- [Interviewer] Foster and jumping around.

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:48.036
- Yeah.

00:00:48.036 --> 00:00:48.869
- [Interviewer] And where was dad?

00:00:48.869 --> 00:00:50.120
- My dad was in and out of prison

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:52.163
and he ended up passing away too as well.

00:00:55.521 --> 00:00:57.330
(People shouting outside)

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:58.163
- [Interviewer] Sorry. (laughs)

00:00:58.163 --> 00:00:58.996
- It's okay.

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:02.943
- [Interviewer] How was your childhood

00:01:02.943 --> 00:01:05.290
with your grandmother and the foster home?

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:06.893
- Well, with my grandmother,

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:09.863
she was abusive.

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:11.623
I was always getting beat,

00:01:11.623 --> 00:01:14.380
and that's what made the
worker come and take me

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:15.690
and remove me from her,

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:19.410
into an actual foster home with
a foster mother and family.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:22.280
And growing up in the foster home,

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:24.810
my foster mom, she was
an ordained minister.

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:29.330
And in the beginning everything
was okay and whatnot.

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:32.264
But as I started getting
older, she started

00:01:32.264 --> 00:01:35.760
saying how I was going to be a prostitute,

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:37.190
how I'm gonna die at an early age,

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:40.030
how my own blood family
is gonna disown me,

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:42.200
how guys are going to beat on me.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.090
To where, when I graduated high school

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:46.430
and I left from her home,

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:47.263
I believed it.

00:01:47.263 --> 00:01:49.070
So everything that she said
that was gonna happen to me,

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:51.240
except death, has happened.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:52.980
Like, guys will beat on me,

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:54.080
I became a prostitute,

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.080
Because that's all I wanted when I left.

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:59.010
My family disowned me,

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.850
and I came close to death.

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:03.500
I got shot by a client with a BB gun.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:05.100
And so I have buck shots,

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:07.387
and broken fragments in
my face because of it.

00:02:07.387 --> 00:02:09.650
But I fought harder.

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:11.090
It's very, very hard

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:12.680
- [Interviewer] What age did
start working in the street?

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:16.038
- 18, fresh out of high school.

00:02:16.038 --> 00:02:16.871
- [Interviewer] Do work for the pimp,

00:02:16.871 --> 00:02:18.390
or on your own?

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:21.050
- When I first got out, I had (Indistinct)

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:21.970
which was a pimp,

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:24.010
and it didn't work out with him.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.210
I started trying to do
the 'renegade' thing.

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:27.380
I couldn't do it.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:30.430
And then I ended up meeting another guy,

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:31.850
and I was with him for a long time,

00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:34.033
but it was hard to get away from him too.

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:35.973
So, yeah.

00:02:38.411 --> 00:02:39.244
- [Interviewer] Have you
been arrested for this?

00:02:39.244 --> 00:02:40.420
- Yes, I have.

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:42.360
Too many times. (laughs)

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:43.193
Yeah.

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:46.430
- [Interviewer] Are drugs
part of the picture for you?

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:48.080
- Yes.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:48.913
Yes it is.

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:51.292
- [Interviewer] What drugs do you use?

00:02:51.292 --> 00:02:52.250
- Crystal

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:54.903
I never would have thought that

00:02:54.903 --> 00:02:56.210
I would be doing that.

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:57.560
You get what I'm saying?

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:58.899
So, yeah.

00:02:58.899 --> 00:02:59.765
- [Interviewer] Do you have kids?

00:02:59.765 --> 00:03:00.598
- I have four

00:03:00.598 --> 00:03:02.012
- [Interviewer] And are you raising them?

00:03:02.012 --> 00:03:03.517
- No.

00:03:03.517 --> 00:03:05.100
I have two boys and two girls.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:08.600
Two of them, got taken to the system,

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.950
because one of my family
members told on me.

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:13.730
And then the other two, I
just had one in November.

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:15.120
She's with my sister.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.730
And then my one year old is with his dad.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.600
So they're with family, the last two

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:22.337
- [Interviewer] Does
doing this for a living

00:03:22.337 --> 00:03:23.710
get you down sometimes?

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:25.160
- It does.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:26.050
It really does.

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:27.221
It's scary,

00:03:27.221 --> 00:03:28.570
because you never know,

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:29.740
whose car are you going to get into.

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:31.320
Like I said, I got shot before,

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:32.153
Not knowing.

00:03:32.153 --> 00:03:33.270
You get what I'm saying?

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:36.420
It's depressing sometimes.

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:37.253
You go through a lot.

00:03:37.253 --> 00:03:38.580
You never know

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:40.090
like I said, whose car
you're gonna get into?

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:41.340
You never know what's
going to happen to you.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:43.410
And it's a lot that comes with the life.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:44.380
You know?

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:46.000
- [Interviewer] You've
been beaten up and raped?

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.030
- I've been beaten up.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:48.870
I've been raped before,

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:49.703
at gunpoint.

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:54.490
Came close to death numerous times

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:57.873
by the hands of a pimp and a client.

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:00.550
It's scary, you know?

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:01.600
- [Interviewer] What was your relationship

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:02.550
with the pimp like?

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.320
- In the beginning it was okay.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:07.650
But then he uses too.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:10.270
And it got to the point to where

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:14.340
he used to choke me to where
I'd start foaming at the mouth.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:15.870
He'd beat me.

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:17.080
His girl-

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:19.070
I have stab wounds on my arm.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.660
And then when I was pregnant,

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:23.100
his girl stabbed me right
here when I was pregnant

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:25.270
I tried to run from him.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:26.780
He ended up finding me,

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:29.560
and it just went downhill basically.

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:33.095
And it took a lot for me to
get away from him, you know?

00:04:33.095 --> 00:04:36.860
And by that, I ended up
going to where I'm at now.

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:38.780
And because I don't have a pimp,

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:42.560
and I'm working in
someone's hood basically,

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:43.583
they're taxing me.

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:46.090
They see that I don't have nobody.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:47.480
And they don't like
the 'renegading' thing.

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:49.740
So one of the guys there, he beats on me,

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:50.810
he makes me give him money.

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:53.810
And he says, if I don't, he's
gonna crack my skull open.

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:55.180
The other day he stomped me out.

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:56.348
All types of stuff-

00:04:56.348 --> 00:04:57.181
- [Interviewer] You told me last night.

00:04:57.181 --> 00:04:58.400
- Recently, yeah.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:04:59.950
Well, like a couple of days ago

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:01.743
he pulled me out of someone's
car and stomped me out,

00:05:01.743 --> 00:05:04.693
then last night he socked me
and knocked me out last night.

00:05:06.009 --> 00:05:08.243
- [Interviewer] What hours
are you typically working?

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:10.073
- It depends.

00:05:10.073 --> 00:05:12.210
Sometimes from,

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:13.980
like 11 in the afternoon.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:17.010
And I'll go back and
forth and I'll go outside,

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:20.293
and I'll be outside to
like maybe one on and off.

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:23.460
And then I'll go in when
the police gets hot.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:24.293
Yeah.

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:27.610
- [Interviewer] Is it
competitive out on the street

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:28.830
with all the girls out there?

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:31.720
- It used to be when I used
to work the other interstate

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:34.030
like in the 60s, because
it's a lot of competition.

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:36.190
That's why I ended up going
down towards Imperial,

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:38.570
because I don't like to
be around a lot of girls.

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:40.300
Because I feel like that's my competition.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:42.600
When I'm on another end, where
there's not too many girls,

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:44.160
I make my money.

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:45.840
It's better for me that way.

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:46.700
So yeah.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:47.590
- [Interviewer] When you were younger,

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:50.210
did you have dreams of doing
something else with your life?

00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:51.210
- Medical assistant.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:54.010
- [Interviewer] How far
did you go in school?

00:05:54.010 --> 00:05:55.310
- I graduated high school.

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:01.240
Then I ended up going to Kaplan

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:03.260
and I took the medical assisting test

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:04.910
to be a medical assistant
to go to school for it.

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:06.240
I passed it.

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:07.830
Then I found out I was
pregnant with my kid,

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:09.880
my first daughter, and I never went back.

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:12.800
- [Interviewer] And what
stops you from doing it now?

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:13.890
Because you're still young.

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:15.224
- Yeah, um.

00:06:15.224 --> 00:06:16.057
- [Interviewer] How old are you now?

00:06:16.057 --> 00:06:17.171
- 29.

00:06:17.171 --> 00:06:18.004
- [Interviewer] You can still do it.

00:06:18.004 --> 00:06:18.837
- I can.

00:06:18.837 --> 00:06:21.180
It's just being in the streets.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.510
It will take for me to have to get

00:06:22.510 --> 00:06:24.250
out of the area and get away from,

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:25.563
to get my mind right I feel like.

00:06:25.563 --> 00:06:27.720
Because I know I have it in me, you know?

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:31.190
It's just the drugs and I've
been doing this for so long.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:33.253
So it's kind of hard sometimes, you know?

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:36.540
- [Interviewer] What was
the worst time of your life?

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:39.010
- When I got shot in my face with a BB gun

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:42.880
I went on an out call,

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:46.470
not knowing it was more than
one person in the house.

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:47.773
And when I went in there,

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:50.630
the guy took me down the hallway.

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:52.080
And when I came to the first room,

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:54.510
it was another guy standing by the closet.

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:57.100
And someone told me to
turn around and run.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:58.710
But as soon as I turned around to run

00:06:58.710 --> 00:07:00.270
I heard a "BOOM!".

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:01.220
Next thing I'm on the floor,

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:03.070
and I feel like a whole
bunch of warm stuff

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:04.040
coming out of my head.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:05.140
And come to find out,

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:05.973
he shot me with a-

00:07:05.973 --> 00:07:08.180
I think the doctor said a gauge?

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:10.290
It shot out multiple buck
shots and it sprayed me.

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:12.680
So I have Buck shots and broken fragments

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:13.533
all in my face.

00:07:17.015 --> 00:07:18.730
They ended up leaving, the two guys.

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:20.330
Then my friend that was outside

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:21.310
heard it, came in,

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:22.518
and they called 9-1-1.

00:07:22.518 --> 00:07:24.220
And where we were, there
wasn't no trauma center.

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:25.660
So they had to call the helicopter

00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:27.000
and had to airlift me from-

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.660
It was Blythe, California,

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:29.970
to Palm Springs Regional.

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:33.120
I almost died because of it.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:35.570
But now I'm stuck with broken
fragments and buck shots,

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:37.466
still in my face.

00:07:37.466 --> 00:07:38.570
- [Interviewer] Could've
lost your eyes right?

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:39.590
- I could've.

00:07:39.590 --> 00:07:41.090
One actually missed my eye right here.

00:07:41.090 --> 00:07:43.160
It's like, literally like
right here by my eye.

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:44.340
It missed my eye.

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:45.910
And all through here, I have

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:49.533
Broken fragments and a whole
bunch of Buck shots in my face.

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:51.293
So, yeah.

00:07:51.293 --> 00:07:53.407
- [Interviewer] What was
the best time of your life?

00:07:53.407 --> 00:07:55.043
- When I had my kids.

00:07:55.043 --> 00:07:56.894
- [Interviewer] When you had your kids?

00:07:56.894 --> 00:07:57.980
- When I had my kids.

00:07:57.980 --> 00:08:01.070
It just, you know, makes me happy.

00:08:01.070 --> 00:08:05.330
But now that they're not with
me, it kinda sucks, you know?

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:08.280
But I know they're
taken care of, you know?

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:09.113
Yeah.

00:08:09.113 --> 00:08:10.273
- [Interviewer] Do you ever talk to them?

00:08:12.107 --> 00:08:13.922
- No, I can't talk to them.

00:08:13.922 --> 00:08:14.755
Two of them,

00:08:14.755 --> 00:08:16.697
I don't know where they're at
because they got adopted out.

00:08:16.697 --> 00:08:18.143
And my last two,

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:20.700
they're too young to talk.

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:24.380
- [Interviewer] Have
you been in love before?

00:08:24.380 --> 00:08:25.213
- I have

00:08:29.870 --> 00:08:33.370
- My ex folks that I had ran
from, I was in love with him,

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:35.700
but I seen the things
that he was doing to me

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:36.750
and it hurt me.

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:40.960
And it took a lot for me
to get over that, you know?

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:42.420
Because he knows there's
no feelings in life.

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:45.717
There's no feelings, but
I've been in love before.

00:08:45.717 --> 00:08:46.810
- [Interviewer] And
doing this for a living

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:49.430
kinda makes that difficult, right?

00:08:49.430 --> 00:08:50.263
- Yeah, it does.

00:08:51.456 --> 00:08:56.050
A lot of people don't respect
working girls, you know?

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:57.730
they look down on us.

00:08:57.730 --> 00:08:58.563
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:08:58.563 --> 00:09:00.675
They don't realize you
have a heart and a soul

00:09:00.675 --> 00:09:01.508
and a story.

00:09:01.508 --> 00:09:02.341
- Or what we go through

00:09:02.341 --> 00:09:03.760
If they were to put
themselves in our shoes.

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:06.730
Or sit and ask us.

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:08.860
Like just talk to us, period.

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:10.160
They always assume things.

00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:10.993
You get what I'm saying?

00:09:10.993 --> 00:09:12.610
Instead of sitting there
and asking the person,

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:13.700
or talking to a person,

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:15.740
they wanna think this person is like this.

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:17.830
But not until you sit and you ask me,

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:19.190
or anything.

00:09:19.190 --> 00:09:20.390
you're not going to know nothing about me,

00:09:20.390 --> 00:09:21.400
or why I am the way I am.

00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:23.560
That's where people get me twisted.

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:25.830
They think I'm a bad person or
they think I'm this, I'm that

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:26.950
But they never sit down and ask me

00:09:26.950 --> 00:09:29.343
or talk to me to figure
out who I really am.

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:32.843
- [Interviewer] Alright, Jasmine.

00:09:32.843 --> 00:09:34.650
Well, thank you so much
for sharing your story.

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:36.770
And good luck with everything.

00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:38.533
I would love to see you
back with your kids.

00:09:38.533 --> 00:09:39.366
- Thank you.

00:09:39.366 --> 00:09:40.280
- [Interviewer] Thanks, bye.

